    "scope": "Scoped Windows validation for new read-only impact-area classifier, explicit same-snapshot Meaning replay and early CLI dispatch: full library plus26 Git/Meaning/capture/scope/editor/process integration targets, all-target Clippy, Python and mandatory TypeScript checks. No shared impact/Meaning producer, HostGit, Store or source-scope implementation changes. Whole-native, hosted/platform, wider semantic/upstream and full STATUS acceptance remain separate."
  },
  "findings": [
    "Explicit git areas replays the unchanged sealed impact-detail parent and optionally one to four selected saved native Meaning graphs. Workspace, exact base/head snapshot, canonical graph hash and every evidence path/content hash bind membership. Missing, foreign or corrupt requested graphs refuse instead of silently reverting to directory-only output. No source capture, Git/ref access, provider/credential/network call, publication or latest-pointer change occurs.",
    "Exact directory spelling supplies the labeled fallback. Every saved concept, original record/support, broader membership and tied minimum remains visible under graph/packet/concept/side references. Smaller distinct supported-file sets rank first; equal names never merge identities. The parent retains exact UTF8/CRLF quotes, declarations, directed/parallel observations and byte ranges, with occurrence pointers and separate classifications/groups.",
    "New closed limits and fixed ceilings bound paths, occurrence/manifest/concept/evidence/support/membership/assignment counts, selected Meaning artifact bytes, metadata preflight and canonical output. Disjoint payload reservations precede cloning; a final exact bounded writer admits the whole result and CLI newline before stdout. New counters do not pretend to measure inherited replay IO or hard memory/scheduler cost. One owned read view and restored SQL policy preserve current cancellation, deadline and transaction boundaries.",
    "Eight actual saved Git/CAS/SQLite/CLI cases cover immutable parent and every occurrence, exact output-cap admission/refusal, no Git/provider on PATH, working-file deletion, equal-label distinct concept ties, smaller/broader file sets, source/receipt replay, corruption with no fallback, zero/hard limits, caller transaction/SQL/cancel/expiry, unchanged complete Store/CAS/ledger/index state and genuinely empty selected changes. Meaning setup uses an explicitly invoked owned literal Node protocol fixture, removed before offline queries; no live model quality or external provider certification is implied.",
    "Twenty-four separate actual CLI host-input/protocol cases pass on the identical final binary: positive default/explicit files, exact8192/8193 byte boundary, relative/parent/device/ADS and a real unprivileged junction, nested unknown/missing/duplicate/authority-bearing fields, hard maxima, duplicate/too-many Meaning selectors, unused write/snapshot authority, zero timeout/output and fixed non-echoing markers. They are not added to Cargo totals or substituted for symbolic-link prerequisites.",
    "Development preserves a Windows process-lookup failure before Cargo started (zero format/tests), four initial passing cases, a six-case run with two fixture-assumption failures, and corrected six/eight-case passes. The existing Meaning normalizer already merges byte-identical claims; distinct descriptions create two real published equal-label concepts. The fixture state oracle counts its own eight deliberate SQL tamper/restore writes; each area operation independently leaves every table, CAS blob and change count unchanged. No runtime behavior was weakened to correct these fixtures.",
    "This scoped run is not whole-native or current hosted acceptance. Both actual Windows symlink prerequisite failures, inferred semantic identity/ownership, compiler dispatch, merge safety, upstream schema/quality, remaining full STATUS/R1-R9 functionality and original inventory/certifications remain open. No main merge, release, production deployment or public App comment is claimed."
  ],
